✅ If You Installed Jenkins as a Windows Service (recommended):
Automatic Start (on boot):

Jenkins runs automatically in the background as a Windows service.

You can access it at:
👉 http://localhost:8080
(unless you changed the port).

Manually Start Jenkins Service:

Press Windows + R, type services.msc, and hit Enter.

Scroll down to find Jenkins in the list.

Right-click → Start (if it’s not already running).

To restart: Right-click → Restart.

Method: Get Initial Admin Password from Jenkins File
If you're seeing the Jenkins setup screen asking for an administrator password, you can find it here:

📁 Path on Windows:
makefile
Copy
Edit
C:\ProgramData\Jenkins\.jenkins\secrets\initialAdminPassword

 Already Set Up Jenkins and Forgot Password?
If you've already completed the setup and forgot your admin password, you can:

Option 1: Check User Credentials
Go to:

pgsql
Copy
Edit
C:\ProgramData\Jenkins\.jenkins\users\admin\config.xml
Open config.xml and look for:

xml
Copy
Edit
<passwordHash>#jbcrypt:....</passwordHash>
You can't retrieve the actual password from the hash, but this confirms the user exists.

Option 2: Reset Password by Creating New User
Stop Jenkins service.

Edit the file:

arduino
Copy
Edit
C:\ProgramData\Jenkins\.jenkins\config.xml
Find this line and change true to false:

xml
